---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const breadcrumbs = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Editorial Policy' }];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Editorial policy"
  description="How we source, write, verify, review, and correct study resources."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  updated="16 November 2026"
>
  <h2>Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    Our goal is a small, trustworthy library of original, exam-focused study material. We
    prefer a complete subject hub over hundreds of empty pages. Content quality and legal
    safety come before publishing volume.
  </p>

  <h2>Source hierarchy</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Official AKTU syllabus, notices, and question-paper portal (facts and links).</li>
    <li>Open-licensed or public-domain material with clear attribution.</li>
    <li>Our own original writing, examples, diagrams, questions, and solutions.</li>
    <li>Contributor material with a written licence and a named reviewer.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    We do not use competitor notes, publisher textbooks, coaching material, Telegram or
    WhatsApp PDFs, or scans with an unknown licence.
  </p>

  <h2>Clean-room process</h2>
  <p>
    We separate fact extraction from writing. The extraction step records only facts such
    as codes, units, topics, marks, dates, and formulas. The authoring step sees the fact
    sheet, not the copyrighted prose, and writes original explanations, examples, and
    diagrams.
  </p>

  <h2>AI use</h2>
  <p>
    AI may help discover sources, extract facts, draft original explanations, generate
    original diagrams, and run checks. AI does not make the final decision. A human
    subject expert reviews every published resource for accuracy, coverage, and
    originality.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not use AI to rewrite, paraphrase, or re-typeset a copyrighted scan and call it
    original.
  </p>

  <h2>Review and provenance</h2>
  <p>
    Before publication, a resource must pass a similarity check, a fact check, and a human
    review. We record the source, licence, reviewer, review date, and file hash. If a
    resource has no provenance record, it is not published.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections and updates</h2>
  <p>
    When we find an error, we correct it and update the page. When an official rule
    changes, we update the page and the "last verified" date. Significant corrections are
    noted on the page. Report errors through the contact page with a source.
  </p>

  <h2>Dates and official facts</h2>
  <p>
    Dates, circular numbers, eligibility rules, and deadlines are taken from official
    sources. We link the source and advise readers to confirm before acting. We do not
    invent dates, papers, subject codes, or "verified" badges.
  </p>

  <h2>Downloads and advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Free resources have no login, countdown, fake download button, or ad interstitial. If
    ads are enabled, they are clearly separated from the download action. We do not place
    ads on thin, legal, or error pages.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Editorial questions and corrections:
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
